    "result_text": "The full suite passed \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` a helper). **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code right before saving via a new `generateCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (non-letters stripped, so apostrophe/hyphen/space names still yield three letters).\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`) \u2014 a global sequence one more than the current owner count.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it in `toOwnerDto`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and appended the trailing NULL to the hsqldb positional seed inserts (the only positional seed data that tests load).\n\nThe test verifies `SMI-\u2026`/`JON-\u2026` prefixes and that the two consecutive codes' sequence numbers differ by exactly 1 \u2014 both satisfied since the count is read fresh before each save within the transaction.\n\nNote: I did **not** wire `customerCode` into the V2 owner controller \u2014 the spec/test target only `POST /api/owners` (V1). If you want the V2 create path to assign codes too, I can extend it.",
